            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level input TIA branches with DC-overload cancellation must accept inp and inn and preserve the specified input bias and overload behavior.",
            "electrical_reason": "Each input is the emitter of a common-base NPN (Xqcbp/Xqcbn) biased from vb and loaded at ctp/ctn, with an emitter-follower output path to ntp/ntn. The low-pass sensed collector voltages feed differential cancellation pairs Xqdpr/Xqdps and Xqdnr/Xqdns; their dummyp/dummyn outputs are buffered to gdocp/gdocn and drive NMOS shunts Xmdoc_p/Xmdoc_n from inp/inn to ground. Thus the cancellation path acts on DC photocurrent while the RF collector path remains connected. The measured nominal input common mode of 0.7593779 V and overload input voltages also corroborate that the input-bias and DC paths are live."
