            "electrical_reason": "The ntp/ntn signal is AC coupled into the matched first NPN differential stage, whose collectors have RF loads and whose emitter/tail currents are controlled by the three gc-gated NMOS devices. Its collector signals are emitter-follower buffered to n1p/n1n and AC coupled into an electrically analogous second controlled NPN stage terminating at n2p/n2n. This is a continuous two-stage transistor signal path, not passive feedthrough; the measured monotonic gain response confirms that gc reaches the current-steering/control devices. The very low minimum-setting gain is a poor setting outcome, but the topology contains a genuine responsive controlled gain path."
