            "electrical_reason": "There is a real forward signal chain from inp/inn through the TIA, both RF stages, and the output buffer to finalp/finaln, and n2p/n2n also tap the detector inputs. However the detector outputs detp/detn are completely disconnected from the AGC pair, so automatic-mode agc and therefore gc cannot respond to received amplitude. The selector only transfers that detector-independent agc node. Thus the active detector, AGC, and automatic gain-control functions do not form one coherent closed receiver; nominal final-output DC values do not establish the missing control connection."
